      "problem": "What is $\\frac{8a-4b+12}{20b+8a}$ reduced to its lowest terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8a-4b+12}{20b+8a} & =\\frac{4(2a-b+3)}{4(5b+2a)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{4}(2a-b+3)}{\\cancel{4}(5b+2a)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2a-b+3}{5b+2a}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
